cache/
*.ptx
*.jsonl

fusion/*.jsonl
fusion_oracle/*.jsonl
__pycache__/
fusion_real/*.jsonl
fusion_moe/*.jsonl
*/cache/
# README tells a reviewer to run `fusion_oracle/report.py oracle2` for the 6.4% isolation, which
# is the one number in the artifact allowed to be called the cost of bit-exactness. These two
# files are what it reads. They are half a megabyte and they cannot be regenerated without a long
# GPU run, so they ship uncompressed next to their script and that command works as written.
!fusion_oracle/three_way.jsonl
!fusion_oracle/results.jsonl
# The per-row tables are regenerated by `artifact.py --export`; only the summary and the
# machine log ship. Written as a sweep plus two exceptions so a new step's table is covered
# without editing this file.
data/*.csv
!data/summary.csv
!data/env.csv
*.log
